  "worked_solution": "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)=\u27e8{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\frac{5}{{e}^{s-2}},\\,{lim}_{s\\to 2}3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4-2s),\\,{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\,({s}^{3}-5)\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\frac{5}{{e}^{s-2}} & =\\frac{5}{{e}^{0}}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4-2s) & =3{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4-2s) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4-2(0)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u20610 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\,({s}^{3}-5) & ={2}^{3}-5=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)=\u27e85,3,3\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $\u2016f(s)\u2016$ as $s$ approaches $2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\u2016f(s)\u2016 & =\u2016{lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u2016\u27e85,3,3\u27e9\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+9+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{43}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
